    {
      "id": "p02",
      "title": "水的三种状态",
      "kind": "reference",
      "image": "https://pbook-1252924514.cos.ap-guangzhou.myqcloud.com/books/drop/v2/images/02.jpg",
      "text": {
        "en": "States of water. Water can be liquid, called water. Water can be solid, called ice or snow. Water can be gas, called water vapor. Water moves freely from state to state, depending on temperature and pressure. When water evaporates, it moves from liquid to gas. When water condenses, it moves from gas to liquid. When water freezes, it moves from liquid to solid. When water melts, it moves from solid to liquid. When water crystallizes, it moves from gas to solid. When water sublimates, it moves from solid to gas, and skips the whole melting part! The three states of water. My many shapes, moods, and temperatures! Gas. Stretch! Solid. Hold still. Liquid. Go with the flow!",
        "zh": "水的三种状态\n水可以是液态，也可以是固态的冰或雪，还可以是气态的水蒸气。温度和压力变化时，水会改变状态。\n液态变成气态叫蒸发；气态变成液态叫凝结；液态变成固态叫冻结；固态变成液态叫融化；气态直接变成固态叫凝华；固态直接变成气态叫升华。\n气态：伸展开来！固态：保持不动！液态：顺势流动！"
      },
      "audio": {
        "status": "omitted",
        "src": null,
        "reason": "reference-or-cover"
      },
