    {
      "id": "p18",
      "title": "水循环",
      "kind": "reference",
      "image": "https://pbook-1252924514.cos.ap-guangzhou.myqcloud.com/books/drop/v2/images/18.jpg",
      "text": {
        "en": "The water cycle. My favorite big words! Condensation. Precipitation. Evaporation. Infiltration. Collection. Transpiration. More about the water cycle. The water cycle starts with the sun. Energy from the sun lifts water into the air, changing it from liquid to gas. This process of expanding from water to vapor is called evaporation. When water vapor floats around in the air, it is called humidity. Sometimes you can feel how humid the air is when there is a lot of water vapor floating around. Snow and ice can also disappear into the air without melting first. This is called sublimation. As water vapor cools, it forms millions of tiny liquid droplets. This process of turning back to liquid from gas is called condensation. Still floating in the air, these droplets make clouds. When droplets rest on the ground, they make dew. As water droplets squish into each other, they grow. Once they are too heavy to float, they fall as raindrops. Water that falls from the sky is called precipitation. Rain, hail, and snow are all precipitation. When water falls on land, some of it washes off the surface and into streams and rivers, called runoff. Some water soaks into the ground. This is called infiltration. Water that is in the ground is called groundwater. Plants drink in groundwater through their roots, use it to grow, and then release it as vapor from their leaves. This is called transpiration. And when water finds a place to rest in rivers, lakes, oceans, and even in leaves, it is called collection. And then, the whole cycle starts again!",
        "zh": "水循环\n我的最爱：这些大词！\n凝结、降水、蒸发、下渗、汇集、蒸腾。\n\n关于水循环的更多知识\n水循环从太阳开始。太阳的能量把水带到空中，让水从液态变成气态。水变成水蒸气的过程叫蒸发。空气中的水蒸气形成湿度。水蒸气较多时，有时你能感觉到空气很潮湿。雪和冰也能不经过融化，直接进入空气，这叫升华。\n\n水蒸气冷却后形成数以百万计的微小液态水滴，从气态变回液态的过程叫凝结。这些水滴悬浮在空气里，形成云；落在地面物体上时，则形成露水。小水滴相互碰撞、聚合，变得越来越大。当它们重得无法继续悬浮，就作为雨滴落下。\n\n从天空落下的水叫降水，雨、冰雹和雪都属于降水。水落到陆地后，一部分沿着地表流进小溪和河流，叫地表径流；一部分渗入地下，叫下渗。地下的水叫地下水。\n\n植物通过根吸收地下水，用它来生长，再通过叶片以水蒸气的形式释放出去，这叫蒸腾。水在河流、湖泊、海洋，甚至叶片里汇集起来，叫汇集。然后，整个循环重新开始！"
      },
